.TH "UPTERM" "1" "Sep 2026" "Upterm 0.0.0+dev" "Upterm Manual"

.SH NAME
upterm-ci - Host a debugging session from a CI job


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBupterm ci [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Host a terminal session on a CI runner and tell the CI system how to join it.

.PP
This is 'upterm host' with the defaults a CI job needs and a lifecycle suited to
one. There is no terminal on a runner and nobody watching the build log as it
scrolls, so the session:
.IP \(bu 2
accepts clients without an interactive prompt,
.IP \(bu 2
publishes the SSH command the way the CI system expects (on GitHub Actions:
the 'ssh-command' step output, the job summary, and a notice annotation),
.IP \(bu 2
shuts down on its own if nobody connects within --wait-timeout, so an
unanswered session does not hold the runner for the job's whole timeout,
.IP \(bu 2
keeps the session's own terminal output out of the job log, which on a
public repository is public (--log-session-output puts it back),
.IP \(bu 2
ends when a 'continue' file appears, which is how someone inside the
session hands the job back.

.PP
Once a client connects, --wait-timeout no longer applies: the session stays up
until the shell exits, the continue file appears, or the job is cancelled.

.PP
Restrict who may join with --limit-access-to-actor and --limit-access-to-users,
or with any of 'upterm host's own --authorized-user and --authorized-keys flags.
Without one of those, anyone holding the session's SSH command can join, and on
a public repository that command is in a public build log.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--allow-local-tcp-forwarding\fP[=false]
	Allow clients to use SSH local TCP forwarding (ssh -L) through the hosted session, reaching TCP destinations visible to the host.

.PP
\fB--authorized-keys\fP=""
	Specify a authorize_keys file listing authorized public keys for connection.

.PP
\fB--authorized-user\fP=
	Authorize users by fetching their public keys from a code-hosting service. Repeatable. Providers: github, gitlab, codeberg, srht (host optional), gitea, forgejo (host required). Examples: github:alice, github:bob@ghe.example.com, gitea:carol@git.example.com, https://git.example.com/dave

.PP
\fB--continue-file\fP=""
	End the session when this file appears. Defaults to /continue and $GITHUB_WORKSPACE/continue.

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--force-command\fP=""
	Enforce a specified command for clients to join, and link the command's input/output to the client's terminal.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ci

.PP
\fB--hide-client-ip\fP[=false]
	Hide client IP addresses from output (auto-enabled in CI environments).

.PP
\fB--known-hosts\fP="~/.ssh/known_hosts"
	Specify a file containing known keys for remote hosts (required).

.PP
\fB--limit-access-to-actor\fP[=false]
	Authorize only the account that triggered the CI job, by fetching its public keys from the CI system's code host.

.PP
\fB--limit-access-to-users\fP=
	Authorize only these GitHub users, by fetching their public keys. Repeatable, and accepts a comma- or space-separated list.

.PP
\fB--log-session-output\fP[=false]
	Mirror the session's terminal output into the CI job log. Off by default: that log may be public and outlives the run.

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Name this session. Determines the socket paths, so it can be looked up with 'upterm session info NAME'. Defaults to COMMAND-XXXX.

.PP
\fB--no-sftp\fP[=false]
	Disable file transfer via SFTP/SCP. By default, clients can transfer files with the same access as the terminal session.

.PP
\fB-i\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=[~/.ssh/id_{ed25519,ed25519_sk,ecdsa,ecdsa_sk,dsa,rsa}]
	Specify private key files for public key authentication with the upterm server (required). Only existing files are included by default.

.PP
\fB--proxy\fP=""
	HTTP proxy to connect to the server through (e.g. http://proxy.example.com:3128). Works with ssh, ws, and wss servers. Without it, ws and wss connections use HTTPS_PROXY/HTTP_PROXY and ssh connections go direct.

.PP
\fB--pty-size\fP=""
	Pin the session's terminal size as COLSxROWS (e.g. 132x43). Client resize requests are then ignored. Defaults to the host terminal's size, or 80x24 when there is none.

.PP
\fB-r\fP, \fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	Host a read-only session, preventing client interaction. Also restricts SFTP to download-only.

.PP
\fB--server\fP="ssh://uptermd.upterm.dev:22"
	Specify the upterm server address (required). Supported protocols: ssh, ws, wss.

.PP
\fB--skip-host-key-check\fP[=true]
	Automatically accept unknown server host keys and add them to known_hosts (similar to SSH's StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new). This bypasses host key verification for new connections.

.PP
\fB--term\fP=""
	Set TERM for the hosted command. Defaults to the inherited TERM, or xterm-256color when TERM is unset or dumb.

.PP
\fB--wait-timeout\fP=10m0s
	Shut down the session if no client has connected within this long. 0 waits forever.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	enable debug level logging (log file: /home/user/.local/state/upterm/upterm.log).


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Debug a GitHub Actions job, letting only the user who triggered it in:
  upterm ci --limit-access-to-actor

  # Let a named set of GitHub users in, and wait half an hour for one of them:
  upterm ci --limit-access-to-users alice,bob --wait-timeout 30m

  # Hand the job back from inside the session:
  $ touch /continue

  # Use your own upterm server:
  upterm ci --server wss://YOUR_UPTERMD_SERVER --limit-access-to-actor
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBupterm(1)\fP


